# Every path, one owner.
#
# This does not gate anything: enforcement needs branch protection to require review from
# code owners, and GitHub does not accept a maintainer's review of their own pull request,
# so on a single-maintainer repository that setting would make `main` unmergeable. See #60.
#
# What it does earn its place for is the public case: an outside contributor's pull request
# automatically requests review from the owner named here, rather than sitting unnoticed.

